{
  "_comment": "Encounter catalog (real data drives the schema). Each encounter is a named monster roster used by the random-encounter sampler. `area` is the discriminator: \"dungeon\", \"house_basement\", or \"overworld\". `level` is the difficulty band (1–8); the sampler filters by min/max level. `weight` controls the relative pick probability inside an eligible band. `monsters[]` entries are Monster `id` strings (snake_case); duplicates are intentional — they spawn multiple instances of the same monster. `monster_party_tile` is the sprite shown for the lead monster on the overworld map (empty falls back to monsters[0]). v1 nested encounters under area-bucket keys; v2 flattens them into one array. Some v1 encounters share names across areas — those get area-suffixed ids here. Dropped: `terrain` (parsed but no v1 consumer). Optional `custom_map` is a Map `id` — when set, this encounter's battle uses that authored map instead of the default arena.",
